    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Description\n\nThere are multiple LSP commands for TypeScript, such as `vtsls` and `tsgo`. nvim-lspconfig supports `tsgo` from the NPM package [`@typescript/native-preview`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@typescript/native-preview). This package represents the beta rewrite of the TypeScript compiler to Go. It is meant to be used by users who want to try out beta versions of TypeScript 7.0 before it is released.\n\nThis week, TypeScript 7.0 was released. Version 7.0 was rewritten to Go. It ships with LSP support (run `tsc --lsp --stdio`). Install it using the [NPM package `typescript`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/typescript). Now that TypeScript 7.0 has been released, I imagine most users will want to migrate from the beta version (`tsgo`) to the intended stable version (`tsc`).\n\nI suggest that nvim-lspconfig support `tsc --lsp --stdio`.\n\n",
