            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "the lsp in tsgo/tsc7 is not finished yet! The announcement is about the typescript-compiler and not the tsc-lsp.\n> Language service (LSP) \tin progress \tNearly all features implemented.\n\nI think we should wait until they finished their work completely and we know which settings the lsp expects or what the docs says.\nThere is still a open bug regarding `autocompletion of string-types`, that does work in javascript files, but not in typescript files. Every other builtin or custom type is resolveable via completion.\nAnother bug I encountered is the missing lsp signature-help.\n\nI think it's better to wait for the release, that has the finalized lsp to avoid friction.\n",
