            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> the lsp in tsgo/tsc7 is not finished yet! The announcement is about the typescript-compiler and not the tsc-lsp.\n\nThis doesn't seem accurate from my reading of [the announcement](https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-7-0/). They spend quite a bit of time talking about using the language server, without couching it in cautionary \"this isn't ready\" terms.\n\nOf course they are going to continue to work on it, but the announcement very much describes it as ready for use. I think supporting it in this repo makes sense at this stage.\n\nWhether or not the `tsgo.lua` config should simultaneously be removed, or kept for now to avoid disruptions, I don't know.",
