            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Hmm, that was the conclusion what I read in the typescript-go github repo and what I tested today.\nI spend some time today to test the new versions of tsgo (nightly/rc/etc) with the native nvim completion and also mini.completion and clean-like configs... In my opinion the lsp has still bugs, which also other users have encountered. (for example last comment on https://github.com/neovim/neovim/discussions/38042)\n\n@mmirus: Does an updated local version of the tsgo.lua lspconfig work on your system? Without the bug above?\nIf yes, the tsgo config could be updated (it's just about replacing the cmd `tsgo` to `tsc`... the args should be the same.\n\n\n\nAs long as microsoft says:\n> Language service (LSP) in progress Nearly all features implemented.\n\nI'm unsure...\n\nThe problem with an overhasty tsgo => tsc (go) replacement will be, cmds with the same name - the precedence in the $PATH wins. Friction 1,2,3 go.\n",
